one.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/W20/W20_4-Page_MockeryBreeds_Yeren_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/W20/W20_4-Page_MockeryBreeds_Yeren_Interactive.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T01:37:32-08:00","id":1496581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeren gain renown for acquiring power, status symbols, and influence, but do so slowly, for even their handful of spirit-sponsors remain wary of these unnatural creatures. No Yeren has currently advanced beyond Rank Three </div> </div> </div>Yeren have almost all the function of regular changing breeds, only really lacking in that they don't have an animal form. I'm not sure if you'd want to give them a renown section and make things up or encourage the ST to directly use backgrounds (which might be kinda interesting)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T04:18:11-08:00","id":1496586,"title":"","content":"I got no idea if I'd ever let people play those, but really cool you made them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T08:05:50-08:00","id":1496594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494746-mockery-breed-character-sheets?p=1496586#post1496586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got no idea if I'd ever let people play those, but really cool you made them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeren are extremely functional. If you don't mind crossing splats, they're no worse than vampires or Fera.<br /> Kerasi don't have a human form and could maybe pass in a formor game or as someone's monster pet but mostly they don't work.<br /> Aruna and Samsa are more in the camp of -really good formori- rather than changing breed. I like Formori and they have human forms so they're relatively welcome. The cockroaches could even potentially worm their way into a Gaian game (provided, y'know, glass walkers, we're counting them as Gaian right?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 11-09-2022, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T12:02:07-08:00","id":1496617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494746-mockery-breed-character-sheets?p=1496581#post1496581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeren have almost all the function of regular changing breeds, only really lacking in that they don't have an animal form. I'm not sure if you'd want to give them a renown section and make things up or encourage the ST to directly use backgrounds (which might be kinda interesting)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I decided to skip the renown section, and I just went with an extended Other Traits section. Seemed like the way to go. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494746-mockery-breed-character-sheets?p=1496586#post1496586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got no idea if I'd ever let people play those, but really cool you made them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'm glad I could finally get them done. I got the request back in like 2016...lol. But, it was fun making them finally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494746-mockery-breed-character-sheets?p=1496594#post1496594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeren are extremely functional. If you don't mind crossing splats, they're no worse than vampires or Fera.<br /> Kerasi don't have a human form and could maybe pass in a formor game or as someone's monster pet but mostly they don't work.<br /> Aruna and Samsa are more in the camp of -really good formori- rather than changing breed. I like Formori and they have human forms so they're relatively welcome. The cockroaches could even potentially worm their way into a Gaian game (provided, y'know, glass walkers, we're counting them as Gaian right?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, it seems like there is some cool stuff that could be done with em, depending on the story. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T19:03:44-07:00","id":1544764,"title":"","content":"I'd measure the point with <b>samsa gifts</b> on a balancing of factors:<br /> <br /> <b>-</b>Samsa are incapable of gaining renown, and cannot gain gifts from any tribal connection (Lets be honest, even the Glass Walkers are helping them begrudgingly because Cockroach tells them too).<br /> <b>-</b>They'll likely only gain a gift on personal tuitilage with a spirit. (This is possible as cockroach spirits are purposely, <b>going out of their way</b>, trying to help them as stated in Book of the Wyrm).<br /> <b>-</b>They're ONLY going to going to learn gifts outside a caern as its unlikely even the Glass Walkers would let them near one. (Something likely to be overlooked by cockroach spirits; maybe omiting need-of-tribute at least for the first gift for the sake of character creation).<br /> <b>-</b>Samsa cannot learn ANY OTHER gift than what cockroach spirits teach, as stated in <b>BotW </b>(they're still a mockery breed, so only cockroach will help them).<br /> <b>-</b>None of the cockroach taught gifts are below level three.<br /> <b>-</b>It will likely be VERY difficult, if not impossible, for the Samsa to gain another gift. Lacking renown may mean any cockroach spirit will likely demand more in tribute to compensate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Conclusion</b>:<br /> <br /> Something HAS to give for this to be playable; even the possessed had slight modifications to differentiate them from NPC fomori and make them playable.<br /> <br /> So, here is a compromise. Rather than 3 level one gifts at character creation, a starting player Samsa (this wouldn't work with other mockeries) would instead get 1 level three gift.<br /> <br /> Gaining any other gift would be MUCH more difficult and expensive than the equivalent would for a garou, AND they can only gain gift from cockroach spirits. (Gaining new gift for a Samsa could potentially be a significant event for them in the story).<br /> <br /> Learning a gift via a shapechanger mentor would likely work about the same as it would for normal garou, excluding some awkwardness that may make it more difficult.<br /> <br /> Note: really only 2 options of gift, 3 for a metis (which Samsa DO have):<br /> -Intrusion.<br /> -Render Down.<br /> -Wriggle (for metis)<br /> <br /> (Spirit Path is worthless to a Samsa as they are COMPLETELY INCAPABLE of sidestepping into the Umbra, as stated in <b>BotW</b>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27527-devilturnip","user":"Devilturnip","date":". 10-25-2024, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27527-devilturnip","name":"Devilturnip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T09:58:49-07:00","id":1544798,"title":"","content":"Its also worth noting that TECHNICALLY there are rule allowances for Samsa to be part of the Glass Walkers tribe/pack.<br /> <br /> The books state that Cockroach is pushing the GW to help the Samsa, they're helping the Samsa; if begrudgingly.<br /> <br /> Therefore they can, sorta, be part of a Glass Walker led pack. Its not likely they'll be trusted very much, and many may only get token assistance.<br /> <br /> However, it stands to reason that a sufficiently capable &amp; competent Samsa would be accepted out of usefulness (The Glass Walkers are fairly pragmatic; even without cockroach's influence); maybe as a pseudo-packmate or a tribal affiliate.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27527-devilturnip","name":"Devilturnip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T09:27:28-08:00","id":1557419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494746-mockery-breed-character-sheets?p=1494912#post1494912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mockery Breeds will have Rage and Gnosis unless otherwise stated.<br /> <br /> Mockery Breeds don't have any Renown to speak of unless one of the following happen; they become part of Gaia (a huge deal which would be earthshaking, and require great wisdom and hard work from forward-thinking Garou/Fera)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey, the Bastet were created by a Mage, and they're considered part of the Fera. So it's not like there isn't precedent for man-made shifters to be accepted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}